{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/specs/2026-11-15-pose-check-shares-the-federated-material.md .pose/workflows/review.md .pose/rules/security.md .pose/rules/delivery-evidence.md .pose/rules/documentation-style.md; command -v pose; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g POSE.md -g '*bounded-operation*'\"","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-check-shares-the-federated-material\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-15\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on: pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:check-shares-the-federated-material\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-check-shares-the-federated-material\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer o `pose check` conferir uma vez, sob o coordenador, as entradas do índice que todos os escopos consomem (o material federado entre elas), em vez de uma vez por escopo.\n\n### Business value\nFollow-up F1 de `pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once`. Com o pose-dist como dependência federada e o pin em dia, o `check --tolerant` do harne8, que roda no pre-commit, passou de 10 GB em um minuto com 16 workers e levou 37 minutos com 4. Cada escopo recalculava e retinha o material federado inteiro (cerca de 150 s e centenas de MiB de leituras retidas), embora todos consumam a mesma geração do índice.\n\n### Constraints\n- Cada escopo continua com a própria captura e auditoria (D7 do ADR das leituras de governança); só a conferência das entradas do índice consumido passa a ser do coordenador.\n- Uma entrada que muda durante o check reprova a auditoria do coordenador.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Tornar os escopos um único retrato do repositório.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: A scope operation created by a review coordinator shall check the consumed index generation's inputs through the coordinator's operation, computing each input's binding once per (root, generation, producer) for all its scopes.\n- R2: The reads of that shared check shall belong to the coordinator's closure, so an input changed while the scopes run fails the coordinator's audit.\n\n### Non-functional\n- O `pose check --tolerant` do harne8, com o pose-dist em `bf2ff02` e o índice em dia, termina com 16 workers sem passar de 4 GB.\n\n### Security\n- Nenhuma mudança: os escopos já provam o vetor de raízes autorizado do coordenador antes de capturar.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Os veredictos do check não mudam.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `pose/review_operation_view.go`: a operação de escopo recebe a operação do coordenador.\n- `pose/governance_read_view.go`: `checkIndexInputs` delega a ela.\n\n### Artifacts\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_index_inputs_test.go\n- modified: .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:check-shares-the-federated-material module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto em produção por `pose check`, que avalia o fechamento de cada escopo sob um coordenador. Check permanente `check-shares-the-federated-material-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator|TestAScopeIndexInputChangedDuringTheCoordinatorFailsItsAudit|TestGovernanceReadViewScopeCoordinator|TestGovernanceReadViewD7Probe' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- O coordenador passa a reter as leituras do material federado; é uma única retenção, no lugar de uma por worker, e cabe no orçamento de 512 MiB de uma operação.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Delegação da conferência das entradas do índice ao coordenador (R1, R2).\n- [x] Emenda D12 do ADR `governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views`.\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Teste de conferência única e teste de auditoria do coordenador, com prova de reprovação; medição no harne8.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Date: 2026-11-15\n- Context: a conferência das entradas do índice é a mesma para todos os escopos de um coordenador.\n- Options considered: (a) memo de processo do material federado, com chave nas entradas; (b) delegar a conferência ao coordenador, cujo D7 já audita as entradas compartilhadas depois que todos os escopos terminam.\n- Decision: (b), registrada como D12 do ADR.\n- Basis: R1, R2\n- Rationale: (a) precisaria de uma chave que capturasse todas as leituras do material, que não existe hoje; (b) reaproveita a auditoria do coordenador e a interface ciente do vínculo que o D7 exige.\n- Consequences: um check cuja entrada muda durante a execução reprova pela auditoria do coordenador.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nTeste da conferência única e da auditoria; medição numa árvore estável do harne8 (pose-dist em `bf2ff02`, índice em dia), com e sem a mudança.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-15\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26, 16 núcleos; worktree do harne8 com o pose-dist em bf2ff02, o graphforge clonado e as raízes que `scripts/pose-cli-local.sh` injeta; índice gerado logo antes.\n- Notes: `pose check --tolerant` com 16 workers: sem a mudança, abortado em 66 s ao passar de 10,3 GB; com ela, 248 s, pico de 2,5 GB, `SUCCESS` com os 2 avisos de assessment já existentes. Sem a delegação, os dois testes reprovam: os escopos não conferem pelo coordenador, e a entrada mudada passa na auditoria.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: o check do harne8 volta a caber na máquina e termina.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: nenhum.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator check:check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestAScopeIndexInputChangedDuringTheCoordinatorFailsItsAudit\n\n### Known gaps\n- Nenhuma.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\nNão concluída.\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n### Review\n\nRodada 1 (run rrn-162a4fb077dc7c41): o revisor aprovou, e o motor recusou a conclusão no preflight da atestação: o critério `design-causality` mapeava a mudança do ADR para a decisão D1, que não declarava o requisito que a justifica. A D1 passou a declarar `Basis: R1, R2`; nada mais mudou.\n\n# Workflow: Review\n\n## Objective\n\nVerify that a change is correct, production-safe, and aligned with its approved scope and specs.\n\n## Preconditions\n\n- Make the final diff readable through cohesive commits or batches.\n- Provide requirement and spec context.\n- Attach implementer validation evidence, including `pose validate` output.\n- Define acceptance criteria and expected risk.\n\n## Execution checklist\n\n1. Resolve `pose review bundle <scope> --explain` (or `pose_review_bundle`) when bundle policy is enabled; otherwise resolve `pose review-plan <scope> --explain`.\n2. Confirm the semantic scope, patch/tree identity, mapped components and bundle plan digest.\n3. Run required active tools first, evaluate recommended tools explicitly and leave completion-only tools deferred until an attestation exists.\n4. Select the plan's applicable rules explicitly and record them in the review.\n5. Resolve rule conflicts with the most restrictive option, prioritizing security for exposure, authorization, and integrity risks.\n6. Consult `.pose/knowledge/` for relevant handoffs, accepted risks, follow-ups, and decision logs.\n7. Check compliance with specs, contracts, and local instructions.\n8. Review functional correctness and edge cases.\n9. Evaluate security, observability, and performance risks.\n10. Require validation evidence from `.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json` proportional to risk.\n11. Identify regression and rollout or rollback risks.\n12. Run plan-selected assessments, including tech-debt and integration when applicable.\n13. Classify findings by severity and propose objective actions.\n14. **Produce a handoff** in `.pose/knowledge/` when findings result in accepted risk, post-merge monitoring, or deferred work (`pose new-knowledge handoff <slug>`); link it from the review.\n15. Seal the validated subject with `pose review bundle <scope> --seal`; stop if any input is unclassified or changed since preparation.\n16. Issue a final decision: approved, approved with reservations, changes requested, or rejected.\n17. Record the decision with `pose review attest <bundle-id> ... --plan-digest <sha256> --apply`; signed external envelopes use `pose review attest --envelope <path> --apply`.\n18. Run `pose review verify <scope>` and `pose review-check <scope>`; reject stale, incomplete, conflicting or transitively invalid reused criteria.\n19. Apply closeout only after verification reports `ready-to-close`; lifecycle, state and report refreshes must not change the sealed bundle.\n20. When Contributor Mode is active and review identifies linter false-positives, diagnostic frictions, or POSE rule gaps, stage an improvement proposal via `pose contribute stage --type enhancement`.\n\n## Required rule selection\n\nAttach this section to the review:\n\n```md\n## Rules applied during review\n- Change type: <feature|bugfix|refactor|documentation-update|mixed>\n- Workflow consulted: `.pose/workflows/<file>.md`\n- Rules selected:\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/security.md`\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` (extension `pose-rule-backend-go`, when installed)\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/frontend-react.md` (extension `pose-rule-frontend-react`, when installed)\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/kubernetes.md` (extension `pose-rule-kubernetes`, when installed)\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`\n  - [ ] `.pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md` when knowledge or process changes\n- Rationale for each selected rule: <one line per item>\n- Rules not applicable: <list and explain>\n```\n\n## Recurrence escalation\n\n- Trigger `.pose/workflows/recurrence-escalation.md` when recurring rework is uncovered and the threshold is met.\n- Require `recurrence_rework_uncovered` evidence for the 30-day period.\n- Require explicit links from the specialized workflow to applicable domain rules.\n- Require a formal keep, adjust, or discard decision after the 45-day pilot.\n\n## Minimum domain coverage\n\n- React UI: apply `frontend-react`, `security`, and `documentation-style`.\n- Go services: apply `backend-go`, `security`, and `documentation-style`.\n- Cluster deployment or infrastructure: apply `kubernetes`, `security`, and `documentation-style`.\n- Process, spec, workflow, rule, or report: apply `documentation-style`, `knowledge-governance`, and security when sensitive data is involved.\n- Cross-stack changes: apply every touched domain rule cumulatively.\n\n## Domain review checklist\n\n### Security\n\n- Confirm authentication, authorization, and least privilege when applicable.\n- Verify that code, configuration, manifests, docs, and logs contain no secrets.\n- Require applicable vulnerability and secret-scanning evidence.\n\n### Contracts\n\n- Confirm compatibility of public HTTP, event, schema, CLI, and file contracts.\n- Validate forward and backward compatibility for rollout and rollback.\n- Require a spec update for contract changes.\n\n### Observability\n\n- Verify structured logs and metrics without sensitive data.\n- Confirm that probes, health checks, and alerts reflect real behavior.\n- Preserve enough traceability for post-deployment diagnosis.\n\n### Validation\n\n- Require lint, typecheck, test, and build coverage proportional to risk.\n- Require executed `pose validate` evidence and relevant results.\n- Record environment limitations and residual validation risks.\n\n## Editorial checklist\n\n- Use imperative, actionable instructions.\n- Keep bullets short and avoid duplicated sections.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- Reference explicit files and paths.\n\n## Required outputs\n\n- A review decision with rationale.\n- The inspected effective plan, its component provenance and tool dispositions.\n- An immutable sealed review bundle and separate attestation bound to its exact digest.\n- A completed rule-selection section.\n- Findings with severity, evidence, and recommendation.\n- Recurrence classification by domain and cause with preventive actions.\n- An explicit statement about public contracts and compatibility.\n- Residual risks and safe-deployment conditions.\n- References to executed checks and collected evidence.\n\n## Complete multi-rule review example\n\n```md\n## Review Summary\n- Decision: approved with reservations\n- Change type: feature (Go API, React UI, and Helm)\n- Workflow: `.pose/workflows/feature.md`\n\n## Rules applied during review\n- `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` (extension `pose-rule-backend-go`): verified handlers, context, and error handling.\n- `.pose/rules/frontend-react.md` (extension `pose-rule-frontend-react`): verified accessibility and explicit loading and error states.\n- `.pose/rules/kubernetes.md` (extension `pose-rule-kubernetes`): verified resources, probes, and immutable images.\n- `.pose/rules/security.md`: verified authorization and absence of secrets.\n- `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`: verified editorial consistency.\n\n## Checks and evidence\n- `pose validate`: passed\n- `go test ./...`: passed in the backend module\n- `pnpm lint && pnpm test`: passed in the frontend module\n- `helm template` and `kubectl apply --dry-run=client`: passed\n\n## Contracts and compatibility\n- Preserved `POST /v1/storage`.\n- Added optional `retentionDays`, preserving backward compatibility.\n\n## Findings\n- Medium: missing queue-saturation alert; add a metric and alert before production.\n- Low: frontend error lacks request-id context; improve observable UX.\n\n## Residual risks\n- Review did not simulate real cluster load.\n- Increase monitoring during the first 24 hours.\n```\n\n## CI failure interpretation\n\n- Treat `POSE check (strict)` as merge-blocking on protected branches.\n- Treat failed required checks in `POSE validate (strict)` as merge-blocking.\n- Attach pipeline artifacts: `pose-check.log`, `pose-validate.latest.log`, and the POSE report.\n- Classify optional-check failures as quality reservations with an owned remediation plan.\n- Reject changes that violate specs, public contracts, security, or safe rollout.\n\n## Phased rollout for unready modules\n\n- Enforce the current required checks immediately.\n- Use `moduleOverrides` to phase adoption without weakening global structural and required gates.\n- Promote optional checks to required by module with an owner and agreed window.\n\n### Optional-to-required promotion protocol\n\n- Select a pilot domain and map candidate checks with owners and explicit risks.\n- Measure success for four weeks and require a baseline of at least 95 percent.\n- Promote only eligible domains through `moduleOverrides`.\n- Update the validation matrix and quality policy in the same change set.\n- Monitor regressions and adjust rollout without removing established required gates.\n- Update specs and rules when rollout changes merge acceptance criteria.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- Resolve or formally accept every critical and high finding.\n- Make the final decision clear and actionable.\n- Support quality and security conclusions with evidence.\n- Preserve approved scope without unjustified drift.\n\n## Reviewer mode\n\n**Objective:** evaluate technical quality and production readiness with emphasis on correctness, risk, and scope.\n\n- **Focus:** functional correctness, spec consistency, regression and security risk, operability, validation quality, and actionable feedback.\n- **Anti-patterns:** approve without sufficient evidence; review style while ignoring functional risk; request unrelated changes; block progress on subjective preference.\n- **Handoff:** state the decision, severity and evidence for each finding, safe merge or deployment conditions, accepted risks, and recommended monitoring.\n# Rule: Security\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for authentication, authorization, sensitive data, external integrations, dependencies, and attack surfaces.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Apply least privilege to resource and credential access.\n- Store secrets only in appropriate secret-management mechanisms, never in code.\n- Validate and sanitize external input for its execution context.\n- Keep personal and confidential data out of plaintext logs and metrics.\n- Evaluate new dependencies for maintenance, licensing, and known vulnerabilities.\n- Test both positive and negative authentication and authorization cases.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Committing credentials, tokens, keys, or secrets in any versioned artifact.\n- Disabling TLS or certificate verification without a formally documented mitigation.\n- Trusting client input for authorization decisions.\n- Executing dynamic commands without adequate validation and escaping.\n- Ignoring critical security alerts without an approved exception record.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run secret scanning on the changed diff or scope.\n- Run the module's applicable dependency vulnerability scanner.\n- Pass the relevant authentication and authorization tests.\n- Complete a review for sensitive-data exposure in logs and configuration.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Delivery Evidence\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when writing or reviewing any document that **claims delivery,\ncompletion, or readiness**: status reports, handoffs, summaries, module READMEs,\ncurrent-state sections in specs or proposals, and messages that say something is complete.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Claim delivery only with attached, verifiable gate evidence: command and output\n  (`pose validate`, `go test`, `tsc`, `vitest`) or a link to the corresponding POSE report.\n- Use POSE lifecycle vocabulary: `draft`, `in-progress`, `done`, `blocked`,\n  `superseded`, or `abandoned`. Do not invent labels such as `completed` or `100% COMPLETE`.\n- Separate **implemented and verified** work from **planned or documented** work.\n  A plan describes intent; do not present that intent as current reality.\n- Reference the report or evidence that crossed the spec exit gate before using `done`.\n- Convert relative dates to absolute dates and stamp the verification date.\n- Declare exact source-tree artifact actions in the spec and reconcile them\n  against an immutable Git change set before claiming delivery.\n- Treat artifact declarations, Git observations and delivery verification as\n  separate evidence; none proves the others by itself.\n- For typed delivery targets, require a path from reconciled artifacts through\n  a production entrypoint to current structured validation results. A surface\n  requires reachability plus integration/e2e evidence; a composed capability\n  requires integration evidence.\n- Evidence answers for the component it ran in or for a component inside it: a\n  module-wide run covers its subtree, but a result from a directory inside a\n  component does not answer for the whole component. Coverage that rests only\n  on a containing module is reported as `inferred-coverage` — name it as such.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Claiming `100% COMPLETE` or production readiness without a green\n  `pose validate --strict` for every affected module.\n- Publishing contradictory delivery documents for the same scope; reconcile them first.\n- Merging code with completion documentation before the applicable POSE checks pass.\n- Mixing aspiration and verified state in one paragraph without clear labels.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `pose check --strict` for structure and spec status enums.\n- Run `pose validate --strict` for every module the document claims to deliver.\n- Run `pose lint-spec` when the document is a spec.\n- Run `pose artifact-check --strict` when the scope changes governed source-tree paths.\n- Run `pose surface-check --strict` for specs with `delivers` and `pose\n  roadmap-check --strict` before a roadmap claims completion.\n- `pose assess discover --if-stale --update-state` when closing specs to update completeness metrics, technical debt, and reports under `.pose/assessments/` and `.pose/state/`.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence over progress narratives when rules conflict.\n- When pressured to claim completion without a gate, record the real state\n  (`in-progress` or `blocked`) and the remaining exit conditions.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Documentation Style\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for process documentation, rules, specs, workflows, and operational instructions.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Write instructions in the imperative mood and begin them with action verbs.\n- Keep bullets short and limited to one idea.\n- Avoid duplicating sections with the same purpose across files.\n- Link to the single source of truth instead of copying its content.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- State each instruction's scope explicitly to reduce ambiguity.\n\n## Examples: good and bad\n\n### Redundancy\n\n- **Good:** \"Update review criteria in `.pose/workflows/review.md` and reference that workflow from the root AGENTS file.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Repeat review criteria in AGENTS, the workflow, and every related spec.\"\n\n### Ambiguous reference\n\n- **Good:** \"Run the lint check described by the review workflow.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Run that standard validation before pushing.\"\n\n## Quick editorial checklist\n\n- Language is imperative and direct.\n- Bullets are short and non-overlapping.\n- Files do not duplicate sections.\n- `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` are used consistently.\n- References point to explicit files or paths.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n/home/go/.local/bin/pose\nAGENTS.md\nPOSE.md\nlocales/pt-BR/POSE.md\nlocales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/AGENTS.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git diff 729501a0b91a4ff6ca5c0aebc46eb0b82ba10128 f2fab49732aae997fe4661761aa69af7d4a71291 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_index_inputs_test.go .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git diff 729501a0b91a4ff6ca5c0aebc46eb0b82ba10128 f2fab49732aae997fe4661761aa69af7d4a71291 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_index_inputs_test.go .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md b/.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\nindex 9e615e1c..8266ee54 100644\n--- a/.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\n+++ b/.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\n@@ -271,3 +271,30 @@ and streamed 1.26 GB in 2,511 reads, then 523 MB again in its audit.\n Streaming bounds memory, not I/O: the bytes read still grow with the\n attributed history.\n \n+\n+## A coordinator checks the consumed index's inputs for its scopes (D12) — 2026-11-15\n+\n+Spec `pose-check-shares-the-federated-material` refines D7. Under one\n+coordinator, every scope consumes the same pinned index generation, and its\n+inputs (the federated material among them) are the same for every scope.\n+D7 made each scope recompute them inside its own capture. With the\n+pose-dist corpus as a federated dependency, the federated material of one\n+harne8 check costs about 150 s and several hundred MiB of retained reads.\n+Each of 16 workers recomputed and retained it: `pose check --tolerant`\n+passed 10 GB within a minute, and four workers took 37 minutes.\n+\n+A scope operation created by a coordinator delegates its check of the\n+consumed index's inputs to the coordinator operation. The bindings are\n+computed once per (root, generation, producer), through the coordinator's\n+Files and charged to its budget. The coordinator's final audit, which D7\n+already runs after every scope joins, covers those reads. A scope's own\n+closure keeps everything else it reads. An input that changes while the\n+scopes run fails the coordinator's audit, so the gate fails: no scope is\n+judged against a freshness check its closure does not cover. Measured on\n+harne8: 248 s at a 2.5 GB peak with 16 workers, against an abort past\n+10 GB.\n+\n+This shares one immutable answer (whether the consumed generation's inputs\n+are current) in the binding-aware way D7 requires: scopes already prove the\n+coordinator's authorized root vector before a capture. It does not make the\n+scopes one snapshot.\ndiff --git a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\nindex e4b559e0..e0ee32c1 100644\n--- a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n+++ b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n@@ -2398,6 +2398,13 @@\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/pose\", \"-run\", \"TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator|TestAScopeIndexInputChangedDuringTheCoordinatorFailsItsAudit|TestGovernanceReadViewScopeCoordinator|TestGovernanceReadViewD7Probe\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n+        },\n         {\n           \"name\": \"federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\",\n           \"program\": \"go\",\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\nindex 41246405..be037243 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\n@@ -90,6 +90,13 @@ type governanceReadViewRoot struct {\n }\n \n type governanceReadViewOperation struct {\n+\t// indexInputsFrom, when set, is the coordinator operation a scope\n+\t// operation was created under: the scope's check of the consumed index's\n+\t// inputs is the coordinator's, read through the coordinator's Files and\n+\t// audited when every scope has joined (ADR\n+\t// governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views D12).\n+\tindexInputsFrom                   *governanceReadViewOperation\n+\tindexInputsFiles                  Files\n \tprimary                           *governanceReadView\n \troots                             []*governanceReadViewRoot\n \tinitialRoots                      map[string]string\n@@ -634,6 +641,9 @@ func (op *governanceReadViewOperation) checkIndexInputs(files Files, root, produ\n \tif op == nil || pin == nil || pin.Status != IndexGenerationCurrent {\n \t\treturn nil\n \t}\n+\tif from := op.indexInputsFrom; from != nil && from != op {\n+\t\treturn from.checkIndexInputs(op.indexInputsFiles, root, producer, pin)\n+\t}\n \tabs, err := filepath.Abs(root)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn []string{\"index input root could not be resolved\"}\n@@ -677,9 +687,14 @@ func (op *governanceReadViewOperation) checkIndexInputs(files Files, root, produ\n \treturn reasons\n }\n \n+// governanceIndexInputBindingObserved sees each computation of an index\n+// input's binding; tests count them.\n+var governanceIndexInputBindingObserved = func(root, name string) {}\n+\n // Revalidation must use the same captured project/resolver context as the\n // generation consumer, including when that consumer is a foreign Store.\n func (op *governanceReadViewOperation) indexInputBinding(files Files, root, producer, name string) (string, bool) {\n+\tgovernanceIndexInputBindingObserved(root, name)\n \tif name != \"federated-material\" {\n \t\treturn IndexInputBindingIn(files, root, name)\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\nindex 9b8f34e9..032c8a01 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n@@ -649,6 +649,14 @@ func (s Store) WithReviewScopeOperationView(run func(Store) error) error {\n \t\treadView.markUnknown(\"review-operation\", \"scope authorized root vector differs from coordinator\")\n \t\treturn errors.Join(errGovernanceReadViewOutsideRoot, reviewOperationGovernanceAuditError(readView.audit(), readView, nil))\n \t}\n+\t// The consumed index's inputs, the federated material among them, are the\n+\t// same for every scope of the coordinator: they are checked once, under\n+\t// the coordinator's view, whose audit runs after every scope joins (ADR\n+\t// governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views D12).\n+\tif coordinatorView, _ := governanceReadViewFromFiles(parent.coordinatorStore.fsys()); coordinatorView != nil && coordinatorView.operation != nil {\n+\t\treadView.operation.indexInputsFrom = coordinatorView.operation\n+\t\treadView.operation.indexInputsFiles = parent.coordinatorStore.fsys()\n+\t}\n \tview := &reviewOperationView{root: filepath.Clean(shared.Root), files: shared.fsys(), project: shared.FederatedProjectID, resolver: shared.FederatedResolver,\n \t\tcoordinator: parent, specUsed: parent.specUsed, specErr: parent.specErr, specFallback: parent.specFallback, specEntries: parent.specEntries, specBySlug: parent.specBySlug,\n \t\tspecBodySeen: make([]bool, len(parent.specEntries)), specBodyDigests: make([][32]byte, len(parent.specEntries)),\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_index_inputs_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_index_inputs_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..b3574188\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_index_inputs_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"sync\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+)\n+\n+func currentPinFixture() *IndexGenerationView {\n+\tinputs := map[string]string{}\n+\tfor _, name := range IndexInputNames {\n+\t\tinputs[name] = \"sha256:bound\"\n+\t}\n+\treturn &IndexGenerationView{Status: IndexGenerationCurrent, Descriptor: IndexGenerationDescriptor{GenerationID: \"gen-fixture\", Inputs: inputs}}\n+}\n+\n+// ADR governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views D12: under one\n+// coordinator, the consumed index's inputs are checked once, through the\n+// coordinator's operation, however many scopes consume the index.\n+func TestScopeIndexInputsAreCheckedOncePerCoordinator(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, _ := d7ProbeCoordinatorRoot(t)\n+\tvar mu sync.Mutex\n+\tcomputed := map[string]int{}\n+\toriginal := governanceIndexInputBindingObserved\n+\tgovernanceIndexInputBindingObserved = func(_, name string) {\n+\t\tmu.Lock()\n+\t\tcomputed[name]++\n+\t\tmu.Unlock()\n+\t}\n+\tdefer func() { governanceIndexInputBindingObserved = original }()\n+\tpin := currentPinFixture()\n+\terr := (Store{Root: root}).WithReviewCoordinator(func(shared Store) error {\n+\t\tcoordinatorView, _ := governanceReadViewFromFiles(shared.fsys())\n+\t\tvar wg sync.WaitGroup\n+\t\terrs := make(chan error, 3)\n+\t\tfor i := 0; i < 3; i++ {\n+\t\t\twg.Add(1)\n+\t\t\tgo func() {\n+\t\t\t\tdefer wg.Done()\n+\t\t\t\terrs <- shared.WithReviewScopeOperationView(func(scope Store) error {\n+\t\t\t\t\tview, _ := governanceReadViewFromFiles(scope.fsys())\n+\t\t\t\t\tif view.operation.indexInputsFrom != coordinatorView.operation {\n+\t\t\t\t\t\treturn errors.New(\"the scope does not check its index inputs through the coordinator\")\n+\t\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\t\tview.operation.checkIndexInputs(scope.fsys(), scope.Root, \"review-operation\", pin)\n+\t\t\t\t\treturn nil\n+\t\t\t\t})\n+\t\t\t}()\n+\t\t}\n+\t\twg.Wait()\n+\t\tclose(errs)\n+\t\tvar combined error\n+\t\tfor err := range errs {\n+\t\t\tcombined = errors.Join(combined, err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn combined\n+\t})\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, name := range IndexInputNames {\n+\t\tif computed[name] != 1 {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"input %s was computed %d times for three scopes of one coordinator\", name, computed[name])\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// D12: the reads of the shared check belong to the coordinator's closure, so\n+// an input changed while the scopes run fails the coordinator's audit.\n+func TestAScopeIndexInputChangedDuringTheCoordinatorFailsItsAudit(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, _ := d7ProbeCoordinatorRoot(t)\n+\tpolicy := filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"policy\", \"review.json\")\n+\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(policy), 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(policy, []byte(`{\"schema_version\":1}`), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tpin := currentPinFixture()\n+\terr := (Store{Root: root}).WithReviewCoordinator(func(shared Store) error {\n+\t\tif err := shared.WithReviewScopeOperationView(func(scope Store) error {\n+\t\t\tview, _ := governanceReadViewFromFiles(scope.fsys())\n+\t\t\tview.operation.checkIndexInputs(scope.fsys(), scope.Root, \"review-operation\", pin)\n+\t\t\treturn nil\n+\t\t}); err != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn err\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn os.WriteFile(policy, []byte(`{\"schema_version\":2}`), 0o600)\n+\t})\n+\tif !errors.Is(err, ErrGovernanceReadViewChanged) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an index input changed under the coordinator passed its audit: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,190p' POSE.md; sed -n '1,230p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; sed -n '580,800p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; sed -n '1,250p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go; sed -n '480,740p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,190p' POSE.md; sed -n '1,230p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; sed -n '580,800p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go; sed -n '1,250p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go; sed -n '480,740p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\"","aggregated_output":"# POSE — Project Operating Standard for Engineering\n\n## 1) What it is\n\nPOSE is the operating standard for agent work in **{{PROJECT_NAME}}**.\n\nPrimary goals:\n\n- reduce ambiguity in tasks\n- improve execution predictability\n- make validation and reporting consistent\n- scale collaboration in a heterogeneous repository\n\nPOSE does **not** replace product architecture or existing security policies;\nit organizes how agents execute technical work.\n\nThe short agent contract lives in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md); this document is\nthe operating manual (structure, CLI, per-type flows, CI, governance).\n\n---\n\n## 2) Principles\n\n1. **Scope first**: read only the instructions and artifacts needed for the affected directories.\n2. **Plan before implementing**: non-trivial changes go through a spec/plan.\n3. **Incrementalism**: small, cohesive, auditable deliveries.\n4. **Deterministic validation**: prefer reproducible commands (`test`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `build`, contract/security checks).\n5. **Risk transparency**: always surface gaps and human-review points.\n\n---\n\n## 3) Structure\n\n```text\n.pose/\n  workflows/     # procedure per work type\n  templates/     # spec.md, roadmap.md, knowledge.md, changelog-fragment.md, doc-audit-report.md\n  rules/         # domain rules (cumulative)\n  knowledge/     # handoffs and notes with active governance\n  adr/           # architectural decisions\n  roadmaps/      # governed roadmaps (milestone DAGs)\n  changelogs/    # pending fragments plus immutable version archives/notes\n  releases/      # version manifests and append-only lifecycle evidence\n  indexes/       # repo-map, services, packages, validation-matrix, module-metadata, task-map, spec-graph, roadmaps\n  reports/       # versionable reports + history JSONL + archive/\n  specs/         # living specs per feature\n  schema-version # instance contract version (see `pose update`)\n\n.agents/skills/  # skills (source of truth; Codex-native format)\n.claude/skills/  # Claude Code-compatible symlinks\npose             # native Go binary available on PATH\nAGENTS.md        # short operating contract\nPOSE.md          # this manual\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4) Key files\n\n- [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md): short contract, precedence and entry points.\n- Subproject `AGENTS.md` (when present): local guidance, applied only to that directory's scope.\n- [`.pose/workflows/*.md`](.pose/workflows/): procedure per work type (`feature`, `bugfix`, `review`, `refactor`, `documentation-update`, `recurrence-escalation`).\n- [`.pose/rules/*.md`](.pose/rules/): domain rules; recurring content lives in [`.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md`](.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md).\n- [`.pose/templates/spec.md`](.pose/templates/spec.md): the single per-feature spec template.\n- `.pose/project.json`: the project's declared identity, `{\"schema_version\":1,\"project_id\":\"proj.<name>\",\"name\":\"…\"}`, written by `pose install` and seeded by `pose update` from the id an older instance declared in `.mcp.json` or `AGENTS.md`. Resolution reads `POSE_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID`, then a `POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS` binding, then this file, then the directory name; a binding that disagrees with the file is refused as `conflicting-project-binding`, a malformed file as `invalid-project-id`, and `pose doctor` reports both under `project.identity`. Declared once, the id is the same in every checkout, under any directory name, for the CLI and the MCP server.\n- [`.pose/templates/roadmap.md`](.pose/templates/roadmap.md): governed roadmap template.\n- [`.pose/templates/changelog-fragment.md`](.pose/templates/changelog-fragment.md): user-facing fragment per spec (written at closeout).\n- [`.pose/workflows/release.md`](.pose/workflows/release.md): immutable release preparation, publication reconciliation and verification.\n\nRelease cuts use `pose release plan`, `prepare`, `check`, `notes`, `record`,\n`status`, `open-next` and `backfill`. A tag is not publication; terminal release\nconfidence comes only from provider and independent-verification evidence.\n- [`.pose/templates/doc-audit-report.md`](.pose/templates/doc-audit-report.md): template for editorial reviews and documentation audits.\n- `pose` binary: native scaffold/check/validate/report automation and MCP server.\n- [`.pose/specs/*/spec.md`](.pose/specs/): living specs per feature.\n- Native project-state artifact, generated by `pose state init` (`pose state`/`pose_project_state`) — optional, absent on a freshly-installed project; configurable staleness policy (optional, defaults 7 days / 20 commits — see §6).\n- [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/): 11 skills in Codex-native format (`name`/`description` frontmatter, body with Required reading + Steps + Output requirements, optional metadata in `agents/openai.yaml`). Use `description` as the single routing source; Claude Code consumes the symlinks in [`.claude/skills/`](.claude/skills/) without requiring `when_to_use`.\n\n---\n\n## 5) Flows per task type\n\nThe operational step-by-step lives in the workflows. Each workflow also\nincludes the relevant \"Execution — planner/implementer/reviewer mode\" sections.\n\n- Feature: [`.pose/workflows/feature.md`](.pose/workflows/feature.md)\n- Bugfix: [`.pose/workflows/bugfix.md`](.pose/workflows/bugfix.md)\n- Review: [`.pose/workflows/review.md`](.pose/workflows/review.md)\n- Refactor: [`.pose/workflows/refactor.md`](.pose/workflows/refactor.md)\n- Documentation: [`.pose/workflows/documentation-update.md`](.pose/workflows/documentation-update.md)\n- Recurrence escalation: [`.pose/workflows/recurrence-escalation.md`](.pose/workflows/recurrence-escalation.md)\n\nThe agent contract (precedence, spec/ADR/check obligations, verification,\ndon'ts) lives in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) and is **not** repeated here.\n\n### 5.1 Spec lifecycle\n\nEvery spec created by `pose new-spec`\ncarries frontmatter with state and dates, preventing specs that linger \"open\"\nafter completion and follow-ups that rot into dead text.\n\n```yaml\n---\nslug: <feature-slug>\nstatus: draft        # draft → in-progress → done | blocked | superseded | abandoned\ncreated_at: 2026-01-15   # stamped by pose new-spec\ncompleted_at:            # filled on the transition to done\nsupersedes:              # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:              # prerequisites: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\npriority:                # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority)\n---\n```\n\n- **`status`** evolves `draft` → `in-progress` → `done`. Alternative terminal\n  states: `superseded` (use `supersedes:` on the successor) and `abandoned`.\n  `blocked` is not terminal: it is an operational condition a spec can leave.\n  Readiness keeps a blocked spec not ready, still resolves its `depends_on`\n  and reports `cause: dependency` or `cause: unknown`; spec transfer also uses\n  `blocked` while a destination is staged. It is never a delivery outcome, and\n  no command rewrites a legacy `blocked` spec to `in-progress`.\n- **`created_at`/`completed_at`** give the spec's real time window (file mtime\n  is unreliable — it changes on every edit).\n- **`depends_on`** declares prerequisites as an **inline comma-separated\n  list** (POSE frontmatter is flat by contract — never a multi-line YAML\n  list), with typed refs: a spec slug, `milestone:<roadmap>/<id>` or\n  `roadmap:<slug>`. Spec refs are resolved by `check` (existence + graph\n  acyclicity); `milestone:`/`roadmap:` refs resolve against the governed\n  roadmaps in `.pose/roadmaps/` when they exist. `depends_on` expresses a real\n  technical/logical prerequisite; scheduling preference is `priority`'s job.\n  The aggregated graph lives in\n  [`.pose/indexes/spec-graph.json`](.pose/indexes/) (generated by\n  `pose index`; frontmatter stays authoritative) and a spec's eligibility is\n  queryable via the pose-mcp tool `pose_spec_readiness`.\n- **`priority`** (optional) orders attack preference among eligible specs; it\n  creates no blocking.\n- **Follow-ups with disposition:** the `Final Report > Follow-ups` section is\n  not free text. Each item gets a bracketed disposition — `[open]`,\n  `[spawned: <slug>]`, `[covered: <slug>]`, `[duplicate: <slug>]`, `[done]`,\n  `[wont-do: <reason>]`. That answers, per follow-up, whether it seeded a new\n  spec, is already covered elsewhere, was triaged before, or was discarded.\n  Open items additionally declare ownership and a triage service level with a\n  trailing `(owner:@alias crit:low|medium|high review:YYYY-MM-DD)` group —\n  the SLA is a triage promise, not an implementation deadline. That group is\n  the only format read: it must be the last thing on the bullet, in\n  parentheses, and the bullet may wrap. Ownership written any other way is\n  ignored, so the item reads as `unowned` and never becomes overdue;\n  `pose lint-spec` warns about it. Legacy items without the group are reported\n  as `unowned` (warning at closeout).\n- **Requirement trace:** at closeout, the `Validation > Requirement trace`\n  subsection maps every declared `R<N>` to its outcome — `[satisfied]` with\n  evidence (free text plus structured refs `check:`, `test:`, `report:`,\n  `commit:`), `[waived: <reason>]` or `[withdrawn: <reason>]`. Orphaned or\n  missing IDs fail `lint-spec --strict`; the MCP tool\n  `pose_requirement_trace` exposes the bidirectional projection. A `test:` ref\n  must name a test that exists in the repository, its submodules or a nested\n  module repository the validation matrix registers: a Go test function or\n  subtest, a JavaScript/TypeScript test title (exact or in slug form), a Python\n  `test_` or Rust `#[test]` function, a tracked test file, or a `go test -run`\n  pattern that selects a test. An unresolved ref fails `lint-spec` and\n  `pose close` while the spec is open, and is only reported on a closed spec.\n\nCloseout is an explicit step (skill [`pose-spec-closeout`](.agents/skills/pose-spec-closeout/SKILL.md)):\nset `status: done`, fill `completed_at`, triage every follow-up and pass the\ngate `pose lint-spec <slug> --strict`,\nwhich blocks \"done without `completed_at`\" and \"done with an undispositioned\nfollow-up\". The aggregated live backlog (`pose followups --open`) feeds the\nplanning of new specs.\n\nFollow-up triage has **two layers**, by design, to keep the CLI deterministic\nand avoid cascading drift:\n\n1. **Deterministic (CLI):** `pose followups`\n   proposes near-duplicate candidates by lexical similarity. Reproducible, no\n   network, runs in CI.\n2. **Semantic + confirmation (agent):** the `pose-spec-closeout` skill judges\n   intent equivalence (what lexical heuristics miss) and **confirms with the\n   user before writing** the consequential dispositions\n   (`[spawned]`/`[covered]`/`[duplicate]`) — reusing a follow-up is a\n   decision, not a default.\n\n---\n\n## 6) The `pose` CLI\n\n```bash\npose help                          # show help\n\n# Scaffold and specs\npose init [--wizard [--yes]]       # install here when no instance exists (installer\n                                   # flags pass through), else confirm it is installed;\npackage pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n\t\"encoding/hex\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"io/fs\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"reflect\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tGovernanceReadViewSchemaVersion = 1\n\tgovernanceReadViewParserVersion = \"pose-governance-inputs-v1\"\n\tgovernanceReadViewMaxRecords    = 40000\n\tgovernanceReadViewMaxInputBytes = 512 * 1024 * 1024\n\tgovernanceReadViewMaxMetadata   = 16 * 1024 * 1024\n\tReadViewFreshnessCurrent        = \"current\"\n\tReadViewFreshnessUnknown        = \"unknown\"\n)\n\n// GovernanceReadViewMaxInputBytes is the captured-input budget of one\n// governance read view, capture and audit alike (ADR\n// governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views, D10).\nconst GovernanceReadViewMaxInputBytes = governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes\n\nvar errGovernanceReadViewWrite = errors.New(\"pose: governance read view is read-only\")\nvar errGovernanceReadViewFinalized = errors.New(\"pose: governance read view is finalized\")\nvar errGovernanceReadViewOutsideRoot = errors.New(\"pose: governance read view input escapes the project root\")\nvar errGovernanceReadViewBudget = errors.New(\"pose: governance read view budget exceeded\")\nvar errGovernanceReadViewIsDirectory = errors.New(\"is a directory\")\n\n// ReadViewMetadata identifies the inputs verified for one operation. Root\n// paths are represented by digests to avoid disclosing host paths.\ntype ReadViewMetadata struct {\n\tSchemaVersion  int               `json:\"schema_version\"`\n\tID             string            `json:\"id\"`\n\tScope          string            `json:\"scope,omitempty\"`\n\tFreshness      string            `json:\"freshness\"`\n\tEngineVersion  string            `json:\"engine_version\"`\n\tParserVersions map[string]string `json:\"parser_versions\"`\n\tBindings       []ReadViewBinding `json:\"bindings\"`\n\tObservedInputs int               `json:\"observed_inputs\"`\n\tInputBytes     int64             `json:\"input_bytes\"`\n\tLimitations    []string          `json:\"limitations,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// ReadViewBinding is one authorized root in an operation's generation vector.\ntype ReadViewBinding struct {\n\tProjectID       string `json:\"project_id\"`\n\tRootDigest      string `json:\"root_digest\"`\n\tSourceRevision  string `json:\"source_revision\"`\n\tIndexGeneration string `json:\"index_generation,omitempty\"`\n}\n\ntype governanceReadView struct {\n\troot          string\n\tbase          Files\n\tmu            sync.Mutex\n\tcond          *sync.Cond\n\tclosed        bool\n\tactive        int\n\tfiles         map[string]*governanceReadFileObservation\n\tobserved      map[string]*governanceReadObservation\n\tunknown       map[string]map[string]bool\n\tinputBytes    int64\n\tmetadataBytes int64\n\toperation     *governanceReadViewOperation\n}\n\ntype governanceReadViewRoot struct {\n\tproject         string\n\troot            string\n\trevision        string\n\tindexGeneration string\n\tindexPin        *IndexGenerationView\n\tstore           Store\n\tview            *governanceReadView\n\tready           chan struct{}\n\tproducers       map[string]bool\n}\n\ntype governanceReadViewOperation struct {\n\t// indexInputsFrom, when set, is the coordinator operation a scope\n\t// operation was created under: the scope's check of the consumed index's\n\t// inputs is the coordinator's, read through the coordinator's Files and\n\t// audited when every scope has joined (ADR\n\t// governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views D12).\n\tindexInputsFrom                   *governanceReadViewOperation\n\tindexInputsFiles                  Files\n\tprimary                           *governanceReadView\n\troots                             []*governanceReadViewRoot\n\tinitialRoots                      map[string]string\n\tinitialConflicts                  map[string]bool\n\trootProjectByPath                 map[string]string\n\trootRegistryID                    string\n\tallowMissingPrimarySourceRevision bool\n\t// rebuildsIndex is set for the one operation that computes the index set from its sources:\n\t// it reads nothing from the published generation, so a generation that is unavailable\n\t// does not make its closure unknown (spec pose-index-recovery-and-close-scope-consistency).\n\trebuildsIndex    bool\n\tcurrentRoots     func() (map[string]string, map[string]bool, bool)\n\tresolver         ArtifactResolver\n\tbaseStore        Store\n\tmainProject      string\n\tindexPins        map[string]*IndexGenerationView\n\tindexInputChecks map[string]*governanceReadViewIndexInputCheck\n\tunknown          map[string]map[string]bool\n\trootOverflow     bool\n\tregistryOverflow bool\n\tfinalAudits      map[*governanceReadView]governanceReadViewAudit\n\tbudgetMu         sync.Mutex\n\tinputBytes       int64\n\tstreamedBytes    int64\n\tmetadataBytes    int64\n\trecords          int\n\tdirectoryEntries int\n\tgit              *governanceReadViewGitState\n\tmu               sync.Mutex\n}\n\ntype governanceReadViewIndexInputCheck struct {\n\tready   chan struct{}\n\treasons []string\n}\n\ntype governanceReadFileObservation struct {\n\tbytes     []byte\n\treadLimit int64\n\terr       error\n\terrText   string\n\tsource    string\n\tbaseName  string\n\tinfo      fs.FileInfo\n\twitness   fs.FileInfo\n\trootReal  string\n\tresolved  string\n\tproducers map[string]bool\n}\n\ntype governanceReadObservation struct {\n\tmethod     string\n\tpath       string\n\tbaseName   string\n\terr        error\n\terrText    string\n\tinfo       fs.FileInfo\n\twitness    fs.FileInfo\n\tentries    []string\n\tdirEntries []fs.DirEntry\n\tvalue      string\n\tproducers  map[string]bool\n}\n\ntype governanceReadViewAudit struct {\n\tChangedPaths     []string\n\tChangedProducers map[string]bool\n\tUnknownProducers map[string][]string\n}\n\ntype governanceReadViewAuditBudget struct {\n\tinputBytes int64\n\tmetadata   int64\n\trecords    int\n}\n\nfunc (b *governanceReadViewAuditBudget) reserve(metadata int64) bool {\n\tif b == nil || metadata < 0 || b.records+1 > governanceReadViewMaxRecords || metadata > governanceReadViewMaxMetadata-b.metadata {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tb.records++\n\tb.metadata += metadata\n\treturn true\n}\n\nfunc (b *governanceReadViewAuditBudget) reserveInput(bytes int64) bool {\n\tif b == nil || bytes < 0 || bytes > governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes-b.inputBytes {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tb.inputBytes += bytes\n\treturn true\n}\n\nfunc (b *governanceReadViewAuditBudget) reserveDirectory(entries []fs.DirEntry, maxEntries int, maxMetadata int64) bool {\n\tif b == nil || len(entries) > maxEntries || len(entries) > governanceReadViewMaxRecords-b.records {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tmetadata := readViewDirMetadataBytes(entries)\n\tif metadata > maxMetadata || metadata > governanceReadViewMaxMetadata-b.metadata {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tb.records += len(entries)\n\tb.metadata += metadata\n\treturn true\n}\n\ntype governanceReadViewProof struct {\n\troot        string\n\tinputBudget int64\n\tentries     []governanceReadProofEntry\n\tbase        Files\n\tchildren    []*governanceReadViewProof\n}\n\ntype governanceReadProofEntry struct {\n\tmethod     string\n\tpath       string\n\tbaseName   string\n\tdigest     string\n\terrText    string\n\tinfo       fs.FileInfo\n\twitness    fs.FileInfo\n\trootReal   string\n\tresolved   string\n\tinputBytes int64\n\treadLimit  int64\n\tentries    []string\n\tvalue      string\n\tproducers  []string\n}\n\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) remainingInput() int64 {\n\tif op == nil {\n\t\treturn governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes\n\t}\n\top.budgetMu.Lock()\n\tdefer op.budgetMu.Unlock()\n\treturn governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes - op.inputBytes\n}\n\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) reserveInput(size int64) bool {\n\tif op == nil {\n\t\treturn size >= 0 && size <= governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes\n\t}\n\tif size < 0 {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\top.budgetMu.Lock()\n\tdefer op.budgetMu.Unlock()\n\tif size > governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes-op.inputBytes {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\top.inputBytes += size\n\treturn true\n}\n\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) finishInput(reserved, actual int64) {\n\tif op == nil || actual >= reserved {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\top.budgetMu.Lock()\n\top.inputBytes -= reserved - actual\n\tif op.inputBytes < 0 {\n\t\top.inputBytes = 0\n\t}\n\top.budgetMu.Unlock()\n}\n\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) reserveRecord(metadataBytes int64) bool {\n\tif op == nil {\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\top.budgetMu.Lock()\n\tdefer op.budgetMu.Unlock()\n\tif op.records+op.directoryEntries+1 > governanceReadViewMaxRecords || metadataBytes < 0 || metadataBytes > governanceReadViewMaxMetadata-op.metadataBytes {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\top.records++\n\top.metadataBytes += metadataBytes\n\treturn true\n}\n\n// checkIndexInputs verifies the declared source bindings only when a producer\n// actually consumes a derived index. Taking a pin for snapshot identity alone\n// does not make the projection depend on that index, so the projection producer\n// deliberately skips this check. The work is shared per root, generation and\n// producer; each producer still records its own observations and limitation.\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) checkIndexInputs(files Files, root, producer string, pin *IndexGenerationView) []string {\n\tif op == nil || pin == nil || pin.Status != IndexGenerationCurrent {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tif from := op.indexInputsFrom; from != nil && from != op {\n\t\treturn from.checkIndexInputs(op.indexInputsFiles, root, producer, pin)\n\t}\n\tabs, err := filepath.Abs(root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn []string{\"index input root could not be resolved\"}\n\t}\n\tkey := filepath.Clean(abs) + \"\\x00\" + pin.Descriptor.GenerationID + \"\\x00\" + producer\n\top.mu.Lock()\n\tif op.indexInputChecks == nil {\n\t\top.indexInputChecks = map[string]*governanceReadViewIndexInputCheck{}\n\t}\n\tif prior := op.indexInputChecks[key]; prior != nil {\n\t\tready := prior.ready\n\t\top.mu.Unlock()\n\t\t<-ready\n\t\treturn append([]string(nil), prior.reasons...)\n\t}\n\tcheck := &governanceReadViewIndexInputCheck{ready: make(chan struct{})}\n\top.indexInputChecks[key] = check\n\top.mu.Unlock()\n\n\treasons := []string{}\n\tfor _, name := range IndexInputNames {\n\t\tbound, exists := pin.Descriptor.Inputs[name]\n\t\tif !exists || strings.TrimSpace(bound) == \"\" {\n\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"index generation does not bind input \"+name)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tcurrent, known := op.indexInputBinding(files, root, producer, name)\n\t\tif !known || current == \"\" {\n\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"current index input \"+name+\" could not be bounded\")\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif current != bound {\n\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"index input \"+name+\" changed since generation \"+pin.Descriptor.GenerationID)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treasons = uniqueSorted(reasons)\n\top.mu.Lock()\n\tcheck.reasons = append([]string(nil), reasons...)\n\tclose(check.ready)\n\top.mu.Unlock()\n\treturn reasons\n}\n\n// governanceIndexInputBindingObserved sees each computation of an index\n// input's binding; tests count them.\nvar governanceIndexInputBindingObserved = func(root, name string) {}\n\n// Revalidation must use the same captured project/resolver context as the\n// generation consumer, including when that consumer is a foreign Store.\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) indexInputBinding(files Files, root, producer, name string) (string, bool) {\n\tgovernanceIndexInputBindingObserved(root, name)\n\tif name != \"federated-material\" {\n\t\treturn IndexInputBindingIn(files, root, name)\n\t}\n\top.mu.Lock()\n\tproject, selectedRoot := op.rootForPathLocked(governanceAbsoluteRoot(root), \"\")\n\tconflict := op.initialConflicts[project]\n\top.mu.Unlock()\n\tif project == \"\" || conflict || !sameLexicalRoot(root, selectedRoot) {\n\t\treturn \"\", false\n\t}\n\tresolver := op.resolver\n\tresolver.FS = files\n\tresolver.Roots = op.rootsForProducer(resolver.Roots, files, producer)\n\tresolver.snapshots = nil\n\tresolver.governanceDepthLimit = 8\n\treturn IndexInputBindingForStoreIn(Store{Root: root, FS: files, FederatedProjectID: project, FederatedResolver: &resolver}, name)\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) governanceIndexConsumed(status IndexGenerationStatus, err error, pin *IndexGenerationView) {\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tview, carrier := governanceReadViewFromFiles(s.fsys())\n\tif view == nil || carrier == nil || carrier.producer == \"\" || carrier.producer == \"projection\" {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tproducer := carrier.producer\n\tproject := carrier.project\n\tswitch status {\n\tcase IndexGenerationLegacy:\n\t\tmarkGovernanceReadUnknownForProject(s.fsys(), s.Root, project, producer, \"a legacy index has no bound input generation\")\n\t\treturn\n\tcase IndexGenerationCurrent:\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif pin == nil {\n\t\tpin = s.indexPin\n\t}\n\tif pin == nil {\n\t\tcaptured := s.ReadIndexGeneration()\n\t\tpin = &captured\n\t}\n\tif pin.Status != IndexGenerationCurrent {\n\t\tmarkGovernanceReadUnknownForProject(s.fsys(), s.Root, project, producer, \"the consumed index generation could not be fixed\")\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif view.operation == nil {\n\t\tmarkGovernanceReadUnknownForProject(s.fsys(), s.Root, project, producer, \"the consumed index has no operation-scoped input bindings\")\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tfor _, reason := range view.operation.checkIndexInputs(s.fsys(), s.Root, producer, pin) {\n\t\tmarkGovernanceReadUnknownForProject(s.fsys(), s.Root, project, producer, reason)\n\t}\n}\n\n// adoptCapturedView charges the bounded index-generation read made while a\n// lazy root binding was being initialized. The view is not published to other\n// producers until after this transfer, so the operation's aggregate budget\n// still covers those first reads.\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) adoptCapturedView(view *governanceReadView) error {\n\tif op == nil || view == nil {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tview.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer view.mu.Unlock()\n\tvar records, directories int\n\tvar metadata int64 = view.metadataBytes\n\tfor _, file := range view.files {\n\t\trecords++\n\t\tmetadata += int64(len(\"file\") + len(view.displayPath(file.baseName)) + 64)\n\t}\n\tfor _, observation := range view.observed {\n\t\trecords++\n\t\tif observation.method == \"directory\" {\n\t\t\tdirectories += len(observation.entries)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\top.budgetMu.Lock()\n\tdefer op.budgetMu.Unlock()\n\tif view.inputBytes > governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes-op.inputBytes {\n\t\treturn errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tif records < 0 || op.records+op.directoryEntries+records+directories > governanceReadViewMaxRecords {\n\t\treturn errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\tif metadata < 0 || metadata > governanceReadViewMaxMetadata-op.metadataBytes {\n\t\treturn errGovernanceReadViewBudget\n\t}\n\top.inputBytes += view.inputBytes\n\top.records += records\n\top.directoryEntries += directories\n\top.metadataBytes += metadata\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc (op *governanceReadViewOperation) readDirectory(files Files, name string) ([]fs.DirEntry, error) {\n\tif op == nil {\n\t\treturn readDirGovernanceBounded(files, name, governanceReadViewMaxRecords)\n\t}\n\top.budgetMu.Lock()\n\tdefer op.budgetMu.Unlock()\n\tremainingEntries := governanceReadViewMaxRecords - op.records - op.directoryEntries\npackage pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"reflect\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"sync\"\n\t\"sync/atomic\"\n)\n\ntype reviewHeaderObservation struct {\n\towner      string\n\tloss       *SourceLoss\n\tdigest     [32]byte\n\treadError  string\n\tinputBytes int\n}\n\n// readReviewBundleHeader is the same classification for cached and live reads.\n// A known different owner is skippable only after whole-JSON and ambiguity checks.\nfunc readReviewBundleHeader(files Files, dir, name string) reviewHeaderObservation {\n\trel := filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Join(\".pose\", \"review-bundles\", name))\n\traw, err := files.ReadFile(filepath.Join(dir, name))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tloss := SourceLoss{Producer: \"review-bundles\", Artifact: rel, Kind: LossReadError, Detail: err.Error()}\n\t\treturn reviewHeaderObservation{loss: &loss, readError: err.Error()}\n\t}\n\tresult := reviewHeaderObservation{digest: sha256.Sum256(raw), inputBytes: len(raw)}\n\t// What a bundle's bytes say about their scope is a function of the\n\t// bytes: it is parsed once per content digest, so a governance check\n\t// that reads every bundle for every scope parses each content once\n\t// (spec pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once).\n\tparsed := reviewBundleHeaderParses.get(string(result.digest[:]), func() (reviewBundleHeaderParse, bool) {\n\t\treturn parseReviewBundleHeader(raw, rel), true\n\t})\n\tresult.owner = parsed.owner\n\tif parsed.loss != nil {\n\t\tloss := *parsed.loss\n\t\tloss.Artifact = rel\n\t\tresult.loss = &loss\n\t}\n\treturn result\n}\n\n// parseReviewBundleHeader reads the scope a bundle's bytes declare, or why\n// they declare none.\nfunc parseReviewBundleHeader(raw []byte, rel string) reviewBundleHeaderParse {\n\tvar header struct {\n\t\tPayload struct {\n\t\t\tScope struct {\n\t\t\t\tRef string `json:\"ref\"`\n\t\t\t} `json:\"scope\"`\n\t\t} `json:\"payload\"`\n\t}\n\tvar loss SourceLoss\n\tswitch {\n\tcase json.Unmarshal(raw, &header) != nil:\n\t\tloss = attributeLoss(SourceLoss{Producer: \"review-bundles\", Artifact: rel, Kind: LossParseError, Detail: \"the record is not valid JSON\"}, raw, \"payload\", \"scope\", \"ref\")\n\tcase func() bool { _, _, ambiguous := sniffJSONString(raw, \"payload\", \"scope\", \"ref\"); return ambiguous }():\n\t\tloss = SourceLoss{Producer: \"review-bundles\", Artifact: rel, Kind: LossInvalid, Detail: \"the record names its scope more than once\"}\n\tcase header.Payload.Scope.Ref == \"\":\n\t\tloss = SourceLoss{Producer: \"review-bundles\", Artifact: rel, Kind: LossParseError, Detail: \"the record names no scope\"}\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn reviewBundleHeaderParse{owner: header.Payload.Scope.Ref}\n\t}\n\treturn reviewBundleHeaderParse{loss: &loss}\n}\n\n// reviewBundleHeaderParses keeps, per content digest, the scope a bundle\n// names or why it names none; bounded for a long-running process.\nvar reviewBundleHeaderParses = newKeptCache[reviewBundleHeaderParse](50000)\n\ntype reviewBundleHeaderParse struct {\n\towner string\n\tloss  *SourceLoss\n}\n\ntype reviewOperationView struct {\n\tcoordinator      *reviewOperationView\n\tcoordinatorStore Store\n\tscopeBase        Store\n\tscopeRoots       map[string]string\n\tscopeConflicts   map[string]bool\n\tscopeInit        sync.Once\n\tscopeInitErr     error\n\n\tspecOnce        sync.Once\n\tspecUsed        bool\n\tspecErr         error\n\tspecFallback    bool\n\tspecEntries     []Spec\n\tspecBySlug      map[string]int\n\tspecBodyMu      sync.Mutex\n\tspecBodySeen    []bool\n\tspecBodyDigests [][32]byte\n\tspecConflict    bool\n\troot            string\n\tfiles           Files\n\tproject         string\n\tresolver        *ArtifactResolver\n\tonce            sync.Once\n\tclosed          atomic.Bool\n\tcontextConflict atomic.Bool\n\tused            bool // published by once; consumers call once before inspecting it\n\tdirectoryError  string\n\tinventory       [32]byte\n\theaders         map[string]reviewHeaderObservation\n\tfallback        bool\n\tmaxRecords      int\n\tmaxInputBytes   int\n\tmaxRetainedText int\n}\n\n// WithReviewOperationView shares immutable headers and spec metadata for this\n// callback. Strict loading, ordering, trust and each worker's traversal remain\n// live. Finalization rereads observed bytes before the read can be green.\n// This is not an atomic filesystem snapshot or a write authorization cache.\nfunc (s Store) WithReviewOperationView(run func(Store)) error {\n\tbaseFiles := s.fsys()\n\tkeyable := reflect.ValueOf(baseFiles).Comparable()\n\tbase, readView := s.beginGovernanceReadView()\n\tshared := base.withGovernanceReadView(readView, \"review-operation\")\n\tview := &reviewOperationView{root: filepath.Clean(shared.Root), files: shared.fsys(),\n\t\tproject: shared.FederatedProjectID, resolver: shared.FederatedResolver,\n\t\tmaxRecords: 10000, maxInputBytes: 128 * 1024 * 1024, maxRetainedText: 8 * 1024 * 1024}\n\tvar operationErr error\n\tif !keyable {\n\t\t// Unknown identity cannot safely key the bounded optimization. The\n\t\t// operation still reads through the governance view and receives its\n\t\t// final closure audit; it simply falls back to live catalogue traversal.\n\t\tshared.reviewView = nil\n\t\tshared.specs = nil\n\t\tshared.reviewReuse = nil\n\t\trun(shared)\n\t} else {\n\t\toperationErr = shared.withReviewOperationView(view, run)\n\t}\n\taudit := readView.audit()\n\treturn errors.Join(operationErr, reviewOperationGovernanceAuditError(audit, readView, view))\n}\n\nfunc reviewOperationGovernanceAuditError(audit governanceReadViewAudit, readView *governanceReadView, operationView *reviewOperationView) error {\n\tvar result error\n\tchanged := audit.ChangedProducers[\"review-operation\"] || audit.ChangedProducers[\"projection\"]\n\tif changed {\n\t\tpaths := append([]string(nil), audit.ChangedPaths...)\n\t\tif len(paths) == 0 {\n\t\t\tpaths = []string{\"input closure\"}\n\t\t}\n\t\tresult = fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review inputs changed during operation: %s: %w\", strings.Join(uniqueSorted(paths), \", \"), ErrGovernanceReadViewChanged)\n\t}\n\t// The operation view certifies the bytes and metadata its review producers\n\t// consumed. Projection-only context such as an unavailable HEAD does not\n\t// become a write authorization or a current-generation claim here; any\n\t// unprovable read attributed to this operation still fails closed.\n\tif reasons := audit.UnknownProducers[\"review-operation\"]; len(reasons) > 0 && !reviewOperationReadLossIsCovered(audit, readView, operationView) {\n\t\tresult = errors.Join(result, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review input closure is unknown: %s: %w\", strings.Join(uniqueSorted(reasons), \"; \"), ErrGovernanceReadViewUnknown))\n\t}\n\treturn result\n}\n\n// reviewOperationReadLossIsCovered keeps a stable, unreadable bundle in the\n// operation result as source-coverage loss. ReadReviewBundles reports that\n// loss to its caller, and validate() proves the same file remains unreadable;\n// this wrapper should not turn a localized record loss into a second API error.\n// Other unknown inputs still make the operation result unavailable.\nfunc reviewOperationReadLossIsCovered(audit governanceReadViewAudit, readView *governanceReadView, operationView *reviewOperationView) bool {\n\tif readView == nil || operationView == nil || !operationView.used || operationView.fallback {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tfor _, reason := range audit.UnknownProducers[\"review-operation\"] {\n\t\tif reason != \"input bytes could not be read\" {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treadView.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer readView.mu.Unlock()\n\tcovered := map[string]string{}\n\tfor name, observation := range operationView.headers {\n\t\tif observation.readError == \"\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif observation.loss == nil || observation.loss.Kind != LossReadError {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t\tcovered[filepath.Base(name)] = observation.readError\n\t}\n\tif len(covered) == 0 {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tmatched := 0\n\tfor path, observation := range readView.files {\n\t\tif !observation.producers[\"review-operation\"] || observation.err == nil || os.IsNotExist(observation.err) {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\trel, err := filepath.Rel(operationView.root, path)\n\t\tif err != nil || !strings.HasPrefix(filepath.ToSlash(rel), \".pose/review-bundles/\") {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t\tname := filepath.Base(path)\n\t\tif covered[name] == \"\" || covered[name] != observation.errText {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t\tdelete(covered, name)\n\t\tmatched++\n\t}\n\treturn matched > 0 && len(covered) == 0\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) withReviewOperationView(view *reviewOperationView, run func(Store)) error {\n\ts.reviewView = view\n\ts.specs = nil       // an earlier advisory listing is not this operation's capture\n\ts.reviewReuse = nil // copied worker stores each start their own traversal\n\tdefer view.closed.Store(true)\n\trun(s)\n\t// Join lazy initialization, if any; finalization must follow joined workers.\n\tview.once.Do(func() {})\n\tview.specOnce.Do(func() {})\n\treturn errors.Join(view.validateSpecs(), view.validate())\n}\n\n// prepareReviewOperationRead preserves Store's live-read behavior after an\n// operation view retires, while refusing to borrow an active view under a\n// different root, project, resolver, or Files binding.\nfunc (s Store) prepareReviewOperationRead() (Store, error) {\n\tif s.reviewView != nil && s.reviewView.closed.Load() {\n\t\ts = s.withoutGovernanceReadView()\n\t}\n\treadView, viewFiles := governanceReadViewFromFiles(s.fsys())\n\tif readView != nil {\n\t\treadView.mu.Lock()\n\t\tfinalized := readView.closed\n\t\treadView.mu.Unlock()\n\t\tif finalized {\n\t\t\ts = s.withoutGovernanceReadView()\n\t\t\treadView, viewFiles = governanceReadViewFromFiles(s.fsys())\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif s.reviewView != nil && !s.reviewView.closed.Load() && !s.reviewView.boundTo(s) {\n\t\treturn Store{}, s.refuseReviewOperationContext(readView, viewFiles)\n\t}\n\tif readView != nil && viewFiles != nil {\n\t\tif s.FederatedProjectID != \"\" && viewFiles.project != \"\" && s.FederatedProjectID != viewFiles.project {\n\t\t\treturn Store{}, s.refuseReviewOperationContext(readView, viewFiles)\n\t\t}\n}\n\nfunc (v *reviewOperationView) observeDirectoryError(s Store, err error) {\n\tif v.boundTo(s) {\n\t\tv.once.Do(func() { v.used = true; v.directoryError = err.Error() })\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) reviewBundleHeaders(dir string, entries []os.DirEntry) (map[string]reviewHeaderObservation, error) {\n\tv := s.reviewView\n\tif v == nil || !v.boundTo(s) {\n\t\treturn nil, nil\n\t}\n\tv.once.Do(func() {\n\t\tv.used = true\n\t\tv.inventory = reviewHeaderInventory(entries)\n\t\theaders := map[string]reviewHeaderObservation{}\n\t\tinputBytes, textBytes := 0, 0\n\t\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(entry.Name(), \".json\") {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif len(headers) >= v.maxRecords {\n\t\t\t\tv.fallback = true\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tobservation := readReviewBundleHeader(v.files, dir, entry.Name())\n\t\t\tinputBytes += observation.inputBytes\n\t\t\ttextBytes += len(entry.Name()) + len(observation.owner) + len(observation.readError)\n\t\t\tif observation.loss != nil {\n\t\t\t\traw, _ := json.Marshal(observation.loss)\n\t\t\t\ttextBytes += len(raw)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif inputBytes > v.maxInputBytes || textBytes > v.maxRetainedText {\n\t\t\t\tv.fallback = true\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\theaders[entry.Name()] = observation\n\t\t}\n\t\tv.headers = headers // publish only the complete immutable catalogue\n\t})\n\tif v.directoryError != \"\" || v.inventory != reviewHeaderInventory(entries) {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review inputs changed during operation: bundle directory\")\n\t}\n\tif v.fallback {\n\t\treturn nil, nil\n\t}\n\treturn v.headers, nil\n}\n\nfunc (v *reviewOperationView) validate() error {\n\tif v.contextConflict.Load() {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review inputs changed during operation: Store context\")\n\t}\n\tif v.coordinator != nil || !v.used {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tdir, err := ensureReviewArtifactDirIn(v.files, v.root, \".pose/review-bundles\", false)\n\tvar entries []os.DirEntry\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tentries, err = v.files.ReadDir(dir)\n\t}\n\tif v.directoryError != \"\" {\n\t\tif err != nil && err.Error() == v.directoryError {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review inputs changed during operation: bundle directory availability\")\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review inputs changed during operation: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif reviewHeaderInventory(entries) != v.inventory {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review inputs changed during operation: bundle inventory\")\n\t}\n\tif v.fallback {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t} // no header observations were reused\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(entry.Name(), \".json\") {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tbefore := v.headers[entry.Name()]\n\t\traw, err := v.files.ReadFile(filepath.Join(dir, entry.Name()))\n\t\tif before.readError != \"\" {\n\t\t\tif err != nil && err.Error() == before.readError {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review inputs changed during operation: %s availability\", entry.Name())\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review inputs changed during operation: %s: %w\", entry.Name(), err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif sha256.Sum256(raw) != before.digest {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review inputs changed during operation: %s bytes\", entry.Name())\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// WithReviewCoordinator audits shared selection and catalogue inputs after all\n// scope callbacks join. Findings must be buffered until this method returns.\n// Scope operations certify their own closures, not a simultaneous batch snapshot.\nfunc (s Store) WithReviewCoordinator(run func(Store) error) error {\n\tvar callbackErr error\n\tauditErr := s.WithReviewOperationView(func(shared Store) {\n\t\tv := shared.reviewView\n\t\tif v == nil {\n\t\t\tcallbackErr = fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review coordinator requires comparable Files binding\")\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\treadView, _ := governanceReadViewFromFiles(shared.fsys())\n\t\tv.scopeBase = readView.operation.baseStore\n\t\tv.scopeRoots = readView.operation.initialRoots\n\t\tv.scopeConflicts = readView.operation.initialConflicts\n\t\tv.coordinatorStore = shared\n\t\tcallbackErr = run(shared)\n\t})\n\treturn errors.Join(callbackErr, auditErr)\n}\n\n// reviewScopeCatalogue authorizes reuse against the exact coordinator Store,\n// and creates a separately bound catalogue consumer. It never unwraps Files.\ntype reviewScopeCatalogue interface {\n\tscopeCatalogue(Store) (Store, *reviewOperationView, error)\n}\n\nfunc (v *reviewOperationView) scopeCatalogue(s Store) (Store, *reviewOperationView, error) {\n\tif !v.boundTo(s) || v.coordinator != nil || v.coordinatorStore.reviewView != v {\n\t\treturn Store{}, nil, s.refuseReviewOperationContext(nil, nil)\n\t}\n\tv.scopeInit.Do(func() {\n\t\tshared := v.coordinatorStore\n\t\tv.captureSpecs(shared)\n\t\tif v.specErr != nil {\n\t\t\tv.scopeInitErr = v.specErr\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tdir, err := ensureReviewArtifactDirIn(v.files, v.root, \".pose/review-bundles\", false)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tv.observeDirectoryError(shared, err)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tentries, err := v.files.ReadDir(dir)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tv.observeDirectoryError(shared, err)\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\t_, v.scopeInitErr = shared.reviewBundleHeaders(dir, entries)\n\t})\n\tif v.scopeInitErr != nil {\n\t\treturn Store{}, nil, v.scopeInitErr\n\t}\n\treturn v.scopeBase, v, nil\n}\n\n// WithReviewScopeOperationView evaluates one scope, including recursive children\n// and authorized roots, with an independent bounded capture and final audit.\nfunc (s Store) WithReviewScopeOperationView(run func(Store) error) error {\n\tvar catalog reviewScopeCatalogue = s.reviewView\n\tif s.reviewView == nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review scope requires an active coordinator\")\n\t}\n\tbase, parent, err := catalog.scopeCatalogue(s)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tbase, readView := base.beginGovernanceReadView()\n\tshared := base.withGovernanceReadView(readView, \"review-operation\")\n\tif !sameStringMap(parent.scopeRoots, readView.operation.initialRoots) || !sameBoolMap(parent.scopeConflicts, readView.operation.initialConflicts) {\n\t\treadView.markUnknown(\"review-operation\", \"scope authorized root vector differs from coordinator\")\n\t\treturn errors.Join(errGovernanceReadViewOutsideRoot, reviewOperationGovernanceAuditError(readView.audit(), readView, nil))\n\t}\n\t// The consumed index's inputs, the federated material among them, are the\n\t// same for every scope of the coordinator: they are checked once, under\n\t// the coordinator's view, whose audit runs after every scope joins (ADR\n\t// governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views D12).\n\tif coordinatorView, _ := governanceReadViewFromFiles(parent.coordinatorStore.fsys()); coordinatorView != nil && coordinatorView.operation != nil {\n\t\treadView.operation.indexInputsFrom = coordinatorView.operation\n\t\treadView.operation.indexInputsFiles = parent.coordinatorStore.fsys()\n\t}\n\tview := &reviewOperationView{root: filepath.Clean(shared.Root), files: shared.fsys(), project: shared.FederatedProjectID, resolver: shared.FederatedResolver,\n\t\tcoordinator: parent, specUsed: parent.specUsed, specErr: parent.specErr, specFallback: parent.specFallback, specEntries: parent.specEntries, specBySlug: parent.specBySlug,\n\t\tspecBodySeen: make([]bool, len(parent.specEntries)), specBodyDigests: make([][32]byte, len(parent.specEntries)),\n\t\tused: parent.used, directoryError: parent.directoryError, inventory: parent.inventory, headers: parent.headers, fallback: parent.fallback,\n\t\tmaxRecords: parent.maxRecords, maxInputBytes: parent.maxInputBytes, maxRetainedText: parent.maxRetainedText}\n\tview.specOnce.Do(func() {})\n\tview.once.Do(func() {})\n\tvar callbackErr error\n\toperationErr := shared.withReviewOperationView(view, func(scoped Store) { callbackErr = run(scoped) })\n\taudit := readView.audit()\n\treturn errors.Join(callbackErr, operationErr, reviewOperationGovernanceAuditError(audit, readView, view))\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
