{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git status --porcelain; sed -n '2653,2695p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go; sed -n '260,277p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/index.go; sed -n '135,173p' .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\"","aggregated_output":"func (s Store) GetCloseoutState(ref string) (CloseoutState, error) {\n\treturn withGovernanceReviewReadView(s, \"closeout\", func(store Store) (CloseoutState, error) {\n\t\treturn store.getCloseoutState(ref, true)\n\t}, func(state *CloseoutState, metadata *ReadViewMetadata, audit governanceReadViewAudit) {\n\t\tapplyCloseoutReadView(state, metadata, ref, audit)\n\t})\n}\n\nfunc (s Store) getCloseoutState(ref string, includeFederated bool) (CloseoutState, error) {\n\ts = s.reviewOperation()\n\tscope, err := ParseScopeRef(ref)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn CloseoutState{}, err\n\t}\n\treview, err := s.ReviewCheck(ref)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn CloseoutState{}, err\n\t}\n\tstate := CloseoutState{SchemaVersion: ReviewSchemaVersion, Scope: ref, ScopeDigest: review.ScopeDigest, Review: review, LifecycleDone: true, Blockers: append([]string{}, review.Blockers...)}\n\tstate.VerificationBasis = \"applicable-review-contract\"\n\tif review.BundleID != \"\" {\n\t\tstate.VerificationBasis = \"sealed-review-contract\"\n\t}\n\tif !review.Required {\n\t\tstate.VerificationBasis = \"review-not-required-under-applicable-policy\"\n\t\tstate.Limitations = []string{\"Review is not required under the applicable policy/cutoff; this does not establish a historical execution receipt.\"}\n\t}\n\tvar diagnostics []Diagnostic\n\tfor _, blocker := range review.Blockers {\n\t\tdiagnostics = append(diagnostics, OpaqueDiagnostic(\"review-blocker\", DiagnosticCloseout, blocker))\n\t}\n\tblock := func(d Diagnostic) {\n\t\tdiagnostics = append(diagnostics, d)\n\t\tstate.Blockers = append(state.Blockers, d.Message)\n\t}\n\tchildStore := s\n\t// includeFederated=false already suppresses recursive acceptance. Keep the\n\t// authorized binding: clearing it makes a child borrow its parent's active\n\t// read view under a different Store context.\n\tswitch scope.Kind {\n\tcase \"spec\":\n\t\tsp, err := s.GetSpec(scope.Slug)\n\t\tif err != nil {\nfunc refreshDeliveryIndex(root string, data []byte, stderr io.Writer) {\n\tif posepkg.IsSealedCheckout(root) {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\t_ = os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"indexes\"), 0o755)\n\treceipt, _, err := posepkg.Store{Root: root}.ReplaceIndexOrLegacy(\"delivery-integrity.json\", data)\n\tswitch {\n\tcase err == nil:\n\t\tif receipt.CleanupError != nil {\n\t\t\trender(io.Discard, stderr).Failure(\"pose: retention of old index generations failed: \" + receipt.CleanupError.Error())\n\t\t}\n\tcase receipt.Committed:\n\t\trender(io.Discard, stderr).Failure(\"pose: the delivery index was published as generation \" + receipt.GenerationID + \", but its durability could not be confirmed: \" + err.Error() + \"; run `pose index --verify`\")\n\tdefault:\n\t\trender(io.Discard, stderr).Failure(\"pose: the delivery index was not refreshed: \" + err.Error() + \"; run `pose index`\")\n\t}\n}\n\nAn external writer that changes and restores bytes between audits without\nparticipating in a fencing protocol leaves no proof for hashes or `lstat` to\nobserve. A view may claim content equivalence at final validation, but cannot\nclaim that no transition occurred. Where a gate depends on that transition,\nrequire a participating writer proof/lock; otherwise return `unknown` and do\nnot execute the effect. This is not a transaction across the filesystem.\n\n## Alternatives rejected\n\n- **Hash the whole repository or `.pose` on every call:** hashes are not the\n  actual read closure, read unrelated history, and can miss an ABA transition.\n- **Reuse a report or cache as authorization:** a read-only observation does\n  not reserve inputs or authority for a later effect.\n- **Add a process-wide generation registry or watcher proof:** it cannot cover\n  restarts or external writers and belongs to separately governed runtime\n  work.\n- **Copy all source files into a snapshot:** unbounded eager history and new\n  filesystem semantics duplicate the operation view rather than extending it.\n\n## Consequences\n\nCLI and MCP can expose the same operation identity through their shared\nprojection. Consumers see an additive report schema version; old reports stay\nreadable but lack proof for current authorization. Operation memory and final\naudit work are bounded; overflow or uninstrumented reads can make a producer\nunknown. Validating observed files twice adds I/O, and one retry can rerun the\nread-only producers. Existing B14/B15 writers remain the source of truth for\neffects and index commits.\n\nThe engine does not promise an atomic filesystem snapshot, detect an external\nABA that leaves identical final bytes, or defend against writers that bypass\nPOSE fencing. Such inputs cannot authorize an effect whose contract requires\ntransition evidence. More producers become current only when their read paths,\ncoverage and writer boundaries are explicitly brought under the view.\n\n\n## Accepted amendment — 2026-11-06: bounded multi-scope coordination (D7)\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo runtime defects found. Both prior findings remain and are accepted as low-severity follow-ups: incomplete audit comments and missing production-path/performance evidence.\n\nTargeted tests passed with and without the race detector. Surface-check reported no findings; artifact-check reported existing provenance warnings. The worktree remains clean, and no attestation was recorded.\n\nApplied the Go backend, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed bundle `rvb-c08e22744774efdd` against the supplied range.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\",\n      \"line\": 581,\n      \"summary\": \"Continuation of R2-N1: comments here and at line 636 describe independent scope certification without explaining that consumed-index input checks now belong to the coordinator closure. The D12 comment at lines 652-655 is accurate, and check.go propagates coordinator audit failure, so this is documentation drift rather than a runtime defect.\",\n      \"action\": \"Update both public method comments to describe coordinator certification of shared index-input reads and require consumers to await the coordinator result.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N4\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_index_inputs_test.go\",\n      \"line\": 47,\n      \"summary\": \"Continuation of R2-N2: both new tests invoke checkIndexInputs directly, using a synthetic pin and discarding returned mismatch reasons. They prove memo sharing and coordinator mutation detection, but do not assert those properties through a real current-index consumer. Production wiring is supported by code inspection and broader sealed integrations. The specific harne8 requirement of 16 workers below 4 GB remains supported only by the implementer's reported measurement, without a sealed resource-measurement artifact.\",\n      \"action\": \"Add a regression through GetCloseoutState or pose check using a valid current generation, assert binding reuse and mutation rejection, and retain a reproducible resource-measurement receipt for the specified harne8 configuration.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Read review_operation_view.go:579-581 and :635-636; both comments remain unchanged. Retained as accepted low follow-up N3.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Read review_scope_index_inputs_test.go:47 and :85 and the spec's validation log. Both calls remain direct, and the sealed evidence contains no resource-measurement receipt. Targeted normal and race tests passed. Retained as accepted low follow-up N4.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed all six listed subject paths, the complete implementation diff, spec R1/R2 and D1, ADR D7/D12 and existing limitations, validation registration and results, binding authorization, foreign-root routing, memo synchronization, budgets, error propagation, scope retirement, coordinator finalization, CLI check composition, existing scope/D7 tests, relevant knowledge and adversarial documentation. Ran targeted normal and race tests, context resolution, artifact-check, surface-check, assess-design, suggest-review and recurrence-check. Verified the worktree remained clean. No additional defects established.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified sharing and mutation detection with targeted normal and race tests. Inspected binding checks and final CLI audit propagation. The precise harne8 memory bound and production-path regression coverage remain unresolved evidence assumptions, explicitly accepted as low follow-up N4. Existing ADR limits on external change-and-restore transitions remain applicable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Targeted race tests passed, including parallel scope isolation and binding rejection. Delegation fields are initialized before callback publication; the existing mutex and ready-channel memo publishes completed results safely. The CLI joins scopes before coordinator auditing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No public signature, serialized schema, CLI argument or MCP tool contract changes were introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing missing-binding, unbounded-input and mismatch reasons remain intact. Scope binding rejection, audit unknowns and mutation errors remain fail-closed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected check.go:295-375, scope construction, index consumption and foreign-root routing. Existing coordinator and closeout integrations remain sealed as passing; the narrower coverage gap is accepted under N4.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Binding failures retain named input and generation context; coordinator audit errors propagate to check findings. No new sensitive logging is added.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined exported methods, file formats and CLI composition. The change relocates internal input verification while preserving aggregate gate failure and existing public contracts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Targeted normal and race runs passed. Memo keys still distinguish root, generation and producer; delegation uses coordinator Files; mutation detection is covered by the coordinator audit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-8b97be1d37d0b5a6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 explicitly declares Basis R1, R2. Reusing the existing operation memo removes repeated binding computation, while moving its reads into the coordinator closure preserves final mutation detection. The design assessment reproduced the sealed structural digest.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-e0fdbb6a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"ADR amendment D12 records D1's selected coordinator delegation and final-audit ownership, implementing R1 and R2.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"ADR D12 and the validation registration match runtime behavior; two public method comments omit the shared-audit exception.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected mismatch reasons, audit error wrapping and CLI reporting. Operators still receive bounded input-change or unknown-closure context, and coordinator failure prevents a green gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N4\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 and R2 have passing focused evidence and supporting production wiring. The exact non-functional resource bound lacks independently reviewable sealed measurement evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-8b97be1d37d0b5a6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The six subject paths implement the declared delegation, tests, ADR amendment, validation registration and start record. No unrelated implementation changes or public contract expansion were found.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected root, project, resolver and Files identity checks before scope creation, authorized-root vector equality, bounded read routing and retirement checks. Delegation retains the coordinator's authorized Files and budgets. No new authority bypass, dependency or secret exposure was found.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-8b97be1d37d0b5a6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation reuses the existing operation memo and final audit with two internal fields and a delegation branch. A process-wide cache would require a broader validity key and lifecycle. No watcher, persistent cache or snapshot abstraction was added. This choice would need reassessment if scopes acquired different authorization contexts or results were consumed before coordinator completion.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-check-shares-the-federated-material --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed. Existing repository-wide provenance warnings were reported; no blocking artifact error was reported. The sealed checkout suppresses index refresh.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-8b97be1d37d0b5a6\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed the read-only assessment; all six subject files were observed and its input digest matches the sealed structural evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The discovery command saves assessment and state artifacts. Skipped to obey the explicit no-repository-changes boundary; component and rule selection were inspected read-only.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The command unconditionally saves its integration matrix. Used code inspection, sealed integrations and targeted tests within the no-write boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_scope_index_inputs_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment command unconditionally saves its report. The read-only marker scan found no matching markers in the affected implementation files.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose review bundle spec:pose-check-shares-the-federated-material --explain\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion requires the recorded, verified review conclusion. This task explicitly prohibits recording an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose review bundle spec:pose-check-shares-the-federated-material --explain\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until POSE records and verifies this review; a pre-attestation run cannot certify this conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed; selected backend-go, security and documentation-style.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-check-shares-the-federated-material --strict: one target, 226 results and zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused the sealed strict validation producer evidence. Inspected delivery-validation.json: outcome pass, 226 executed and passed, zero failed or skipped. Did not rerun the repository-writing validation publisher.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused sealed component validation evidence and inspected its registered command and passing result. Independently reran the focused command normally and an expanded selection with -race; both passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
